  "status_text": "One extra signal flip can be the difference between a circuit that fits and an impossible task. Lean checked this for on/off tasks built from pairs of formulas (L-lib-1435). At the tighter NOT limit, a fit exists exactly when the two sets of inputs specified by the formulas are disjoint. Every such fit gives a circuit using only AND and OR that separates the two sets with at most the original number of combining gates. Add one NOT and a circuit with a total combining-gate count at most six times the number of stages fits even when the sets overlap.",
